<title>FRANCE: German trucker injured in French truck strike.</title>
<headline>German trucker injured in French truck strike.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>A German truck driver was seriously injured when striking French truckers stoned his lorry near the eastern town of Chalon-sur-Saone on Monday and he had to undergo emergency surgery, a gendarmerie officer said.</p>
<p>The owner-driver from the Stuttgart area, whose name was not released, was hit in the head as he drove towards a roadblock being set up by strikers. He managed to stop his truck on the hard shoulder and summon assistance.</p>
<p>The driver, who was accompanied by his wife, was taken to a hospital in Chalon-sur-Saone before being transferred to the city of Dijon for surgery, the officer said.</p>
<p>Four French suspects were being held for questioning, he added.</p>
</text>
